# Episode 3: The Missing Witness

Detective D. Torque received an urgent call.

A key witness scheduled to testify in a major corruption trial had disappeared.

Police believed the witness had fled the city.

Torque disagreed.

The witness had left behind his wallet, phone, and car.

Nobody planning to run away would leave everything behind.

Torque searched the witness's apartment.

Hidden inside a book was a handwritten note.

The note mentioned an abandoned motel on the edge of town.

Torque and his team investigated.

Inside Room 308 they found signs of a struggle.

A broken lamp.

Blood on the floor.

And a photograph of the witness speaking with a powerful businessman named Victor Hale.

The witness had uncovered evidence connecting Hale to several illegal operations.

Before he could testify, he was kidnapped.

Following financial records and security footage, Torque tracked the kidnappers to a warehouse outside the city.

The witness was rescued alive.

Three suspects were arrested.

The corruption trial moved forward.

Case Closed.

But among the evidence was a familiar symbol.

The same symbol found in Cases #1 and #2.

Someone was still working behind the scenes.
